{
 "title": "Metadata-mutator sweep, September 2026",
 "source": "Rounds 2 and 3 are npm run sweep -- --blocks 150 --tokens 400 --json. Round 1 predates the command and was the equivalent scan run by hand against the table 0.6.0 shipped. Tokens are sampled from recent mainnet blocks by call frequency and filtered to ERC-20 shape; no third-party token list is used. Each round drew a fresh sample, so the token sets overlap but are not identical.",
 "note": "0.6.0 licensed a scored ABSENT on a 52-token scan and a list of eight spellings, and said the list could not be proved complete. These three rounds are what that assumption was worth. Round 1 found four spellings it had missed and two tokens publishing a verified clean absence their own bytecode contradicts. Round 2, after those four were adopted, found three more spellings and two more such tokens. Round 3, after the whole watchlist was promoted into the table, found none. Two consecutive rounds each producing new spellings is the finding; round 3 is evidence, not proof.",
